Projects referenced for design / architecture inspiration
---------------------------------------------------------

EvoFlow is an independent product. During development we also studied (and in
places adapted ideas from) the following open-source agent projects. Linking
them here is attribution and thanks — it does **not** mean EvoFlow is a fork
of any of them, and it does **not** change this repository's primary license.

* ZCode (Z.AI Co., Ltd.)
  https://github.com/zai-org/ZCode
  Areas that were vendored or substantially adapted into EvoFlow are listed
  in the "ZCode (Apache License 2.0)" section above. Beyond those vendored
  portions, EvoFlow also reused ZCode's design notes (e.g. DESIGN.md) and
  the v4 protocol / projection layout as starting points for EvoFlow's own
  shell task board and chat panes. Some paths retain upstream-oriented
  naming (the `zcode-*` workspace folders) for traceability; see file
  headers and scripts/zcode-vendor-manifest.json where present.

* Hermes Agent (Nous Research)
  https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent
  https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com
  (community nickname in Chinese: 爱马仕)
  Areas we looked at include gateway / IM channels, skills, memory plugins,
  and community-ops surface. Some memory-related paths under
  ``backend/packages/harness/evoflow/agents/memory_plugins/memory_port/``
  retain upstream-oriented naming; see file headers where present.

* OpenClaw
  https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw
  https://openclaw.ai
  (community nickname in Chinese: 小龙虾)
  Areas we looked at include multi-channel personal assistants, skills
  packaging, and gateway-style control-plane patterns.

* OpenAI Codex (CLI / agent tooling)
  https://github.com/openai/codex
  Areas we looked at include coding-agent UX, sandbox helpers, and local
  agent-loop patterns.

* Pipecat (Daily)
  https://github.com/pipecat-ai/pipecat
  BSD 2-Clause License — see licenses/pipecat-BSD-2-Clause.txt.
  EvoFlow's Xiaomi (小V) realtime voice path depends on ``pipecat-ai``
  (Pipeline / VAD / UserTurn / TTSService / AudioContextManager, etc.)
  under ``backend/app/gateway/speech/``. We also studied Pipecat's frame
  pipeline, interruption, and latency-observer patterns when designing
  that voice session. Attribution here is thanks and license notice; it
  does **not** change this repository's primary PolyForm Noncommercial
  license for EvoFlow-authored code.

Other runtime / UI foundations are listed in the README acknowledgements
(LangGraph, LangChain, MCP, Tauri, etc.).

If an attribution is missing or a similarity needs a clearer notice, contact
cloud@evovexai.com or open a GitHub Issue; we will review and update this file.

